An Ordinance to amend the Town of Pine Mountain Ordinance to Regulate and Tax Alcohol; to provide an effective date to repeal all ordinances and parts of ordinances in conflict herewith; and for other purposes.

WHEREAS, the Town of Pine Mountain adopted a comprehensive ordinance to regulate and tax alcohol, which was signed into law on October 12, 2020 (together with all amendments thereto, the “Alcohol Ordinance”);

WHEREAS, on November 9, 2020, the Town of Pine Mountain amended the Alcohol Ordinance to expressly prohibit the home delivery of malt beverages, wine, and/or distilled spirits within the limits of the Town of Pine Mountain as provided for in Georgia House Bill 879;

WHEREAS, on June 14, 2021, the Town of Pine Mountain further amended the Alcohol Ordinance to remove any reference to off-premises liquor licensing and package stores, which are not authorized in the Town of Pine Mountain but were inadvertently included in the Alcohol Ordinance as adopted; and

WHEREAS, the Town of Pine Mountain desires to amend the Alcohol Ordinance to (i) clarify the requirements and criteria considered by the Town of Pine Mountain in granting a license under the Alcohol Ordinance; and (ii) expand the enforcement powers granted to the Town of Pine Mountain Chief of Police and his agents relating to a violation of the Alcohol Ordinance.

NOW THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED BY THE MAYOR AND COUNCIL OF THE TOWN OF PINE MOUNTAIN, HARRIS COUNTY, GEORGIA, AND BY AUTHORITY OF THE SAME, IT IS HEREBY ORDAINED AS FOLLOWS:
